@@ -0,0 +1,106 @@
+# HOMESENSE899 Preference Fixes · Activation and Verification
+
+Prepared 19 November 2026 against Sites version 1923, source
+`5816499f243bff493632d5966efe3e8c8e4991e3`.
+PR #420 is historical and must not be reapplied over this implementation.
+
+## Scope
+
+This patch keeps the existing tables, aggregate totals and unexpired legacy
+comments. It adds no new visitor identifiers, comment collection or public
+report. Production deployment, cleanup execution and access changes are not
+part of this preparation. The tests use only disposable local SQLite storage.
+
+## Implemented
+
+- Explicit optionality and a Continue Without Sharing action. Skipping clears
+  unsent choices and focuses the talk heading. Loading the video is separate.
+- Retry-After cooldowns. A definite first rejection permits editing. An
+  ambiguous response freezes and reuses the original key and payload, even if
+  a later attempt is rejected. Retries stop after 23 hours, before the server's
+  24-hour receipt lifetime. No key or choice is persisted in browser storage.
+- Preference report access requires both a non-empty Sites user ID and the
+  existing configured owner email. No editor or extra account receives access.
+  GET remains read-only and filters expired comments; DELETE remains owner-only
+  and same-origin. Responses use private/no-store, identity Vary and nosniff.
+- Scheduled maintenance emits success/failure events containing only event
+  name, outcome and UTC time. Failure rejects the scheduled task. Cleanup
+  removes only expired comments/receipts and old shared quota rows; aggregate
+  totals and unexpired comments are preserved.
+- The Cloudflare build configuration requests `17 * * * *` (hourly, minute 17
+  UTC). This is a requested trigger, not evidence that Sites installs one.
+- The notice is dated 19 November, distinguishes optional sharing consent from
+  operational safeguards, describes retired comments and states the idle-time
+  retention limitation. Aggregate necessity is reviewed annually and totals
+  deleted when translation planning ends.
+
+## Deployment Gate: Still Pending
+
+Do not publish this patch as part of the audit preparation. Obtain an explicit
+deployment request, refresh the authoritative Site source, then merge this
+bounded change into any newer source. Preserve the current audience, owner
+configuration, records and bindings. Do not deploy from the old review PR.
+
+### Idle-Time Retention
+
+Before claiming scheduled physical deletion:
+
+1. Confirm that the deployed Sites runtime supports and installs the hourly
+   trigger emitted by the Cloudflare build. If it does not, use a supported
+   hosted scheduler and authenticated writer, retaining the owner boundary.
+   Do not create a public or unauthenticated purge route as a workaround.
+2. Run the scheduled entry point in isolated staging with expired and
+   unexpired synthetic comments, receipts and quota rows. Verify that expired
+   rows are gone and unexpired rows and totals are unchanged.
+3. Inspect a successful independently triggered run while no page is open.
+   Configure operational alerting on any failed event and on absence of a
+   success event for two hours. Do not send visitor content to alerts.
+4. Only then replace the conditional notice with the verified schedule and
+   actual deletion bound (expiry plus at most the interval to the next
+   successful run). Explain separately what happens during outages and in
+   provider backups. Do not promise deletion from backups without evidence.
+
+### Identity Boundary
+
+Sites provides signed-in identity via `oai-authenticated-user-id` and
+`oai-authenticated-user-email`. The app relies on dispatch to supply trusted
+values. This code adds a second required identity field but cannot validate
+header provenance itself. Do not change the shared Filofax authorisation helper
+or pin an invented user ID.
+
+In staging, verify anonymous and non-owner requests receive 403, the owner can
+read the report and only the owner can delete a synthetic comment with a
+matching Origin. Verify a caller-supplied identity header cannot impersonate
+the owner through every exposed origin. If stripping cannot be established,
+do not enable the report until a supported verified-identity boundary is used.
+Avoid requesting the production report merely to test this change.
+
+### Edge Abuse Controls
+
+The application still has its atomic shared hourly limit (default 60) and
+24-hour receipt deduplication. They limit growth and duplicate retries; they do
+not establish unique people or stop one caller consuming the entire quota.
+
+Deployment owner action: configure a supported Cloudflare edge rate-limit or
+managed challenge for POST `/api/homesense899/preferences`, retaining the
+shared application bound. Start with a staged rule limiting one source to
+five submission attempts per minute, assess false positives for shared
+networks, then select enforcement. Do not persist IPs in preference tables.
+Check provider processing/retention and update disclosures where needed.
+No edge rule or challenge service was activated by this patch.
+
+### Privacy Operations
+
+Record the deployment date of the revised notice, review aggregate necessity
+annually and remove totals when the translation-planning feature ends. Preserve
+the warning that individual aggregate contributions cannot be retrieved or
+withdrawn. Keep any approved aggregate disclosure sufficiently coarse to
+avoid exposing rare categories. Individual comments never enter public output.
+
+## Local Validation
+
+Run `node --test tests/homesense899-preferences.test.mjs tests/homesense899-sharing.test.mjs`.
+These tests simulate D1 transactions using SQLite. They do not prove production
+migrations, distributed concurrency, gateway header stripping, active triggers,
+alert delivery or edge enforcement. Production records must not be used as
+fixtures. No database migration is required by this patch.
